A listener for the textures the guest uploads and the renderer samples

TextureInterface (gs_interface.hpp) tells an application when a HOST ->
LOCAL transfer has arrived whole, when rendering or a LOCAL -> LOCAL copy
writes VRAM pages, when a CLUT load is queued, and when a cached texture
image is made or dropped. It may also name another image to sample in the
place of a cached one: the cached image's sizes, region and bias stay in
the GS's coordinates, so a finer image of the same texture is read at the
same fractions of it. With no listener set, nothing changes.

The port uses it to write the textures the game draws to a folder and to
draw them from files (pc/gs/mh2tex.cpp).

Applied by tools/setup.sh and tools/setup.ps1 to the pinned paraLLEl-GS
commit (tools/versions.txt). paraLLEl-GS is LGPL-3.0-or-later; this patch
is published with the port under the same license.

